# Installations (#82). Requires a JWT with role Admin/Operator/Sales/Designer (planning)
# or Technician (state changes). Port matches launchSettings.json (http profile).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@token = paste-access-token-here
@installationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Create installation (state Planned)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/installations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "0199f0a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
  "contractId": "0199f0a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000002",
  "supplyPointId": "0199f0a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000003",
  "name": "FVE Rodinný dom Nitra",
  "plannedPowerKwp": 9.6
}

### List installations filtered by state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/installations?state=Planned
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My installations (technician)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/installations?assignedToMe=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Detail with state history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update details
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "FVE Rodinný dom Nitra", "plannedPowerKwp": 10.2, "note": "Plechová strecha" }

### Schedule mounting
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scheduledStart": "2026-11-04", "scheduledEnd": "2026-11-05" }

### Assign technicians (user ids with role Technician)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/technicians
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianIds": ["0199f0a0-0000-7000-8000-0000000000aa"] }

### Change state (allowed targets are in allowedTransitions; otherwise 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/transitions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "targetState": "ComponentsOrdered", "note": "Objednané u dodávateľa" }

### Devices (#83): register a panel (type Panel or Inverter; serial number is globally unique, case-insensitive)
@deviceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "Panel", "serialNumber": "JA2410-000123", "manufacturer": "JA Solar", "model": "JAM54S30-450", "powerW": 450 }

### Register an inverter
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "Inverter", "serialNumber": "FRO-10-778899", "manufacturer": "Fronius", "model": "Symo 10.0-3-M", "powerW": 10000 }

### List installed devices (includeReplaced=true adds replaced ones, type=Panel|Inverter filters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/devices?includeReplaced=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Device detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/devices/{{deviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace a device (old one stays in history as Replaced; 409 if already replaced or the serial is taken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/devices/{{deviceId}}/replace
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "serialNumber": "JA2411-000456", "manufacturer": "JA Solar", "model": "JAM54S30-450", "powerW": 450, "reason": "Defective cell, warranty claim" }

### Replacement history of a device (whole chain, oldest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/devices/{{deviceId}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Strings (#84): define a string (number = strings[].id in telemetry, mpptInput optional)
@stringId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/strings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": 1, "name": "South roof", "mpptInput": 1 }

### Update a string
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/strings/{{stringId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": 1, "name": "South roof", "mpptInput": 2 }

### Put a panel into the string (moves it if it is in another string)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/strings/{{stringId}}/panels/{{deviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Take a panel out of the string
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/strings/{{stringId}}/panels/{{deviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Panel layout: strings with panels, summed power per string, unassigned panels
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/strings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### String detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/strings/{{stringId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete an empty string (409 when it still has panels)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/installations/{{installationId}}/strings/{{stringId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
